Host-side gtest unit tests for crosspoint-reader.

Build and run:

  cmake -S test -B build/test
  cmake --build build/test
  ctest --test-dir build/test --output-on-failure -j

Run a single suite directly:

  cmake --build build/test --target StreamingJsonParserTest
  build/test/streaming_json_parser/StreamingJsonParserTest --gtest_filter='*'

Google Test is fetched via CMake FetchContent on first configure; the pinned
version lives in test/CMakeLists.txt.

Shell-script based tests (suites that cannot be built with the host CMake
toolchain due to embedded-only dependencies):

  bash test/run_epub_css_test.sh

KOReader sync (lib/KOReaderSync) is esp_http_client-based and cannot be built
by this toolchain either. It is covered instead by a pair of offline scripts.
No credentials, no accounts, no third-party server is ever contacted.

  # Every server dialect, end to end against a local mock.
  python scripts/kosync_conformance.py

  # Mapping table only; opens no sockets.
  python scripts/kosync_conformance.py --self-test

scripts/kosync_mock_server.py impersonates the dialects the client has to cope
with -- the reference kosync server, Spring-based services like BookLore that
answer a PUT with 201/204 (crosspoint-reader #2876), bodiless 204s, disabled
registration, a captive portal serving HTML with 200, and a redirecting proxy.
The conformance runner spawns one per dialect and asserts the client's
status -> Error mapping comes out right for each.

To exercise the real C++ client rather than the Python mirror of it, run the
mock on the LAN and point a device at it -- plain HTTP, no TLS, no account:

  python scripts/kosync_mock_server.py --dialect spring --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080
  # device: Settings -> System -> KOReader Sync -> Sync Server URL
  #         http://<your-lan-ip>:8080   (any username/password is accepted)

Every request is logged, so this doubles as a way to see exactly what the
firmware puts on the wire.

The mapping table in the conformance runner is a hand transcription of
KOReaderSyncClient.cpp; there is no automatic link, so change both together.
